# Normalize line endings for every text file: the repo stores LF; Windows
# checkouts get CRLF transparently. Without this, a Windows (often non-dev)
# user sees a wall of "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warnings on every commit.
# git auto-detects binary content (NUL bytes) and leaves it untouched.
* text=auto

# Shell scripts must stay LF on ALL platforms. On Windows, CRLF on a .sh makes
# bash fail on the trailing \r ("$'\r': command not found"). This more-specific
# rule overrides text=auto. The template is distributed by clone/copy.
*.sh text eol=lf
**/bin/* text eol=lf
